<title>ZIMBABWE: Haddon &amp; Sly year share falls, div dips.</title>
<headline>Haddon &amp; Sly year share falls, div dips.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Feb 28, 1997</p>
<p>		 (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		   17.2   vs   28.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    7.0   vs    8.5</p>
<p>    Turnover		    57.6   vs   47.9</p>
<p>    Pre-tax income	     1.2   vs    1.9</p>
<p>    Tax			    0.2   vs    0.5</p>
<p>Full Name: Haddon &amp; Sly Ltd</p>
<p>Note: The company said an anticipated increase in domestic retail spending in the second half of its financial year had not developed. Satisfactory growth was confined mainly to supermarket sales at the expense of higher yielding departments. The spending power of consumers continued to be undermined by high levels of inflation, it said.</p>
<p>-- Harare Newsroom: +2634 72 52 28/9</p>
</text>
